{"version":1,"slug":"organized__Others__Quantitative_Aptitude__General_Quant__SSC_CGL_MOCKS_2025_SSC_SUPER_PRACTICE_39954","path":"organized/Others/Quantitative Aptitude/General Quant/@SSC_CGL_MOCKS_2025_SSC SUPER PRACTICE_39954.html","title":"devgagan","provider":"organized","category":"Others/Quantitative Aptitude/General Quant","durationMinutes":60,"totalQuestions":20,"sectionsLocked":false,"sections":null,"questions":[{"question":"<span class=\"eqt\"><p>The area enclosed by the triangle with vertices (3, -2), (1, 8) and (-4, 3) is:</p></span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\"><p>&#2358;&#2368;&#2352;&#2381;&#2359;&#2379;&#2306; (3, -2), (1, 8) &#2324;&#2352; (-4, 3) &#2357;&#2366;&#2354;&#2375; &#2340;&#2381;&#2352;&#2367;&#2349;&#2369;&#2332; &#2342;&#2381;&#2357;&#2366;&#2352;&#2366; &#2328;&#2367;&#2352;&#2366; &#2325;&#2381;&#2359;&#2375;&#2340;&#2381;&#2352;&#2347;&#2354; &#2361;&#2376;:</p></span>","options":["<span class=\"eqt\">22 sq. unit</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">22 &#2357;&#2352;&#2381;&#2327; &#2311;&#2325;&#2366;&#2312;</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">16 sq. unit</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">16 &#2357;&#2352;&#2381;&#2327; &#2311;&#2325;&#2366;&#2312;</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">30 sq. unit</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">30 &#2357;&#2352;&#2381;&#2327; &#2311;&#2325;&#2366;&#2312;</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">34 sq. unit</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">34 &#2357;&#2352;&#2381;&#2327; &#2311;&#2325;&#2366;&#2312;</span>"],"correct_option_id":2,"solution":"<p>Area enclosed by a triangle with vertices (x<sub>1</sub>, y<sub>1</sub>), (x<sub>2</sub>, y<sub>2</sub>) and (x<sub>3</sub>, y<sub>3</sub>) is:</p><p><img width=275 height=36 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p20476/image015.png\"></p><p>Here, x<sub>1</sub> = 3, x<sub>2</sub> = 1, x<sub>3</sub> = -4, y<sub>1</sub> = -2, y<sub>2 </sub>= 8, y<sub>3</sub> = 3</p><p><img width=345 height=36 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p20476/image016.png\"></p><p>= (1/2) * 60</p><p>= <b>30</b> sq. unit</p>","marks":2,"section":null},{"question":"<span class=\"eqt\"><p>In the following figure, PQ is perpendicular to MN and &#8736; P, &#8736; Q, and &#8736; R of triangle &#8710;PQR are 5x, 4x, and 3x, respectively. If PM is the angle bisector of the &#8736;APB, then what is the value of &#8736;APM?</p><p><img width=273 height=175 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p13721/image004.jpg\"></p></span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\"><p>&#2344;&#2367;&#2350;&#2381;&#2344;&#2354;&#2367;&#2326;&#2367;&#2340; &#2310;&#2325;&#2371;&#2340;&#2367; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306;, PQ, MN &#2346;&#2352; &#2354;&#2306;&#2348;&#2357;&#2340; &#2361;&#2376; &#2324;&#2352; &#2340;&#2381;&#2352;&#2367;&#2349;&#2369;&#2332; &#8710;PQR &#2325;&#2375; &#8736; P, &#8736; Q &#2324;&#2352; &#8736; R &#2325;&#2381;&#2352;&#2350;&#2358;&#2307; 5x, 4x &#2324;&#2352; 3x &#2361;&#2376;&#2306;&#2404; &#2351;&#2342;&#2367; PM, &#8736;APB &#2325;&#2366; &#2325;&#2379;&#2339; &#2360;&#2350;&#2342;&#2381;&#2357;&#2367;&#2357;&#2367;&#2349;&#2366;&#2332;&#2325; &#2361;&#2376;, &#2340;&#2379; &#8736;APM &#2325;&#2366; &#2350;&#2366;&#2344; &#2325;&#2367;&#2340;&#2344;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;?</p><p><img width=\"273\" height=\"175\" src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p13721/image004.jpg\"></p></span>","options":["<span class=\"eqt\">15&deg;</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">15&deg;</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">18&deg;</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">18&deg;</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">10&deg;</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">10&deg;</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">20&deg;</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">20&deg;</span>"],"correct_option_id":0,"solution":"<p>Let &#8736;P = 5x, &#8736;Q = 4x and &#8736;R = 3x</p><p>So, 5x + 4x + 3x = 180</p><p>=&gt; 12x = 180</p><p>=&gt; x = 15</p><p>In straight line APR,</p><p>&#8736; APM + &#8736; MPQ + &#8736; QPR = 180</p><p>=&gt; &#8736; APM = 180  -  90  -  5 * 15 = 15&deg;</p>","marks":2,"section":null},{"question":"<span class=\"eqt\"><p>In a &#916; PQR, PQ = 8 cm and QR = 18 cm. How many possible whole values PR can take?</p></span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\"><p>&#2319;&#2325; &#916; PQR &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; PQ = 8 cm &#2324;&#2352; QR = 18 cm &#2361;&#2376;&#2404; PR &#2325;&#2367;&#2340;&#2344;&#2375; &#2360;&#2306;&#2349;&#2366;&#2357;&#2367;&#2340; &#2346;&#2370;&#2352;&#2381;&#2339; &#2350;&#2366;&#2344; &#2354;&#2375; &#2360;&#2325;&#2340;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;?</p></span>","options":["<span class=\"eqt\">16</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">16</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">17</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">17</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">15</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">15</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">14</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">14</span>"],"correct_option_id":2,"solution":"<p>PQ = 8 cm, and QR = 18 cm</p><p>Sum of PQ and QR = 26 cm</p><p>Difference between PQ and QR = 10 cm</p><p>So, 10 &lt; PR &lt; 26</p><p>Hence, PR can take (26  -  10  -  1 =) 15 whole values.</p>","marks":2,"section":null},{"question":"<span class=\"eqt\"><p>In &#8710; ABC, &#8736; B and &#8736; C are complementary. And &#8736;B - &#8736;C =20&deg;. AD&#8869;BC at D and the bisector of &#8736;A meets BC at E. If the measure of &#8736;DAE = x&deg;, then find the supplementary angle of x.</p></span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\"><p>&#8710;ABC &#2350;&#2375;&#2306;, &#8736;B &#2324;&#2352; &#8736; C &#2346;&#2370;&#2352;&#2325; &#2361;&#2376;&#2306;&#2404; &#8736;B - &#8736;C = 20&deg; &#2361;&#2376;&#2404; AD&#8869;BC, D &#2324;&#2352; &#8736;A &#2325;&#2366; &#2360;&#2350;&#2342;&#2381;&#2357;&#2367;&#2349;&#2366;&#2332;&#2325; BC &#2325;&#2379; E &#2346;&#2352; &#2350;&#2367;&#2354;&#2340;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;&#2404; &#2351;&#2342;&#2367; &#8736;DAE &#2325;&#2366; &#2350;&#2366;&#2346; = x&deg; &#2361;&#2376;, &#2340;&#2379; x &#2325;&#2366; &#2360;&#2306;&#2346;&#2370;&#2352;&#2325; &#2325;&#2379;&#2339; &#2332;&#2381;&#2334;&#2366;&#2340; &#2325;&#2368;&#2332;&#2367;&#2319;&#2404;</p></span>","options":["<span class=\"eqt\">150&deg;</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">150&deg;</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">140&deg;</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">140&deg;</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">160&deg;</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">160&deg;</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">170&deg;</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">170&deg;</span>"],"correct_option_id":3,"solution":"<p><img width=419 height=215 id=\"Picture 7\" src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p14006/image008.jpg\" alt=O78.JPG></p><p>Given that,</p><p>&#8736; B and &#8736; C are complementary. So,</p><p>&#8736; B + &#8736; C = 90&deg;... (1)</p><p>And given,</p><p>&#8736;B - &#8736;C =20 &deg;.... (2)</p><p>From equation (1) and (2),</p><p>We get &#8736; B = 55&deg; and &#8736; C = 35&deg;</p><p>Now, x = (&#8736; B - &#8736; C)/2</p><p>x = (55 - 35)/2</p><p>x = 10</p><p>Supplementary angle of x = 180 - 10 = 170&deg;</p>","marks":2,"section":null},{"question":"<span class=\"eqt\"><p>If AD is altitude to the hypotenuse of a right &#8710; ABC, AB = 15 cm and AC = 8 cm, then find the length of AD (to the nearest whole number).</p></span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\"><p>&#2351;&#2342;&#2367; AD &#2319;&#2325; &#2360;&#2350;&#2325;&#2379;&#2339; &#8710;ABC &#2325;&#2375; &#2325;&#2352;&#2381;&#2339; &#2325;&#2366; &#2358;&#2368;&#2352;&#2381;&#2359;&#2354;&#2306;&#2348; &#2361;&#2376; &#2340;&#2341;&#2366; AB = 15 cm &#2324;&#2352; AC = 8 cm &#2361;&#2376;, &#2340;&#2379; AD &#2325;&#2368; &#2354;&#2306;&#2348;&#2366;&#2312; (&#2344;&#2367;&#2325;&#2335;&#2340;&#2350; &#2346;&#2370;&#2352;&#2381;&#2339; &#2360;&#2306;&#2326;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366; &#2340;&#2325;) &#2332;&#2381;&#2334;&#2366;&#2340; &#2325;&#2368;&#2332;&#2367;&#2319;&#2404;</p></span>","options":["<span class=\"eqt\">5 cm</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">5 cm</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">3 cm</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">3 cm</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">7 cm</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">7 cm</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">6 cm</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">6 cm</span>"],"correct_option_id":2,"solution":"<p><img width=278 height=225 id=\"Picture 9\" src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p14265/image010.jpg\"></p><p>ar (&#8710;ABC) = &frac12; * base * altitude = &frac12; * AB * AC = &frac12; * AD * BC</p><p>AD = AB * AC/BC = 120/17 &#8776; 7 cm</p>","marks":2,"section":null},{"question":"<span class=\"eqt\"><p>In a &#8710;MNO, &#8736;NOM = 45&deg;, &#8736;OMN = 120&deg; and side ON = 18&radic;6 cm, then the length of side MN of &#8710;MNO is equal to:</p></span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\"><p>&#2319;&#2325; &#8710;MNO &#2350;&#2375;&#2306;, &#8736;NOM = 45&deg;, &#8736;OMN = 120&deg; &#2324;&#2352; &#2349;&#2369;&#2332;&#2366; ON = 18&radic;6 cm &#2361;&#2376;, &#2340;&#2379; &#8710;MNO &#2325;&#2368; &#2349;&#2369;&#2332;&#2366; MN &#2325;&#2368; &#2354;&#2306;&#2348;&#2366;&#2312; &#2325;&#2367;&#2360;&#2325;&#2375; &#2348;&#2352;&#2366;&#2348;&#2352; &#2361;&#2376;?</p></span>","options":["<span class=\"eqt\">72 cm</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">72 cm</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">36 cm</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">36 cm</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">36&radic;2 cm</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">36&radic;2 cm</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">18&radic;3 cm</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">18&radic;3 cm</span>"],"correct_option_id":1,"solution":"<p><img width=243 height=192 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p18074/image003.jpg\"></p><p>Given, &#8736;NOM = 45&deg;, and &#8736;OMN = 120&deg;, and side ON = 18&radic;6 cm</p><p>By sine rule, </p><p>ON/sin120&deg; = MN/sin45&deg;</p><p>=&gt; 18&radic;6/(&radic;3/2) = MN/(1/&radic;2)</p><p>=&gt; MN = 36&radic;2 * 1/&radic;2</p><p>=&gt; MN = 36 cm</p>","marks":2,"section":null},{"question":"<span class=\"eqt\"><p>UV and SW are two medians of a triangle &#8710;STU, which intersect each other at right angle at point C. Find the length of UW, if lengths of UV and SW are 72 cm and 42 cm respectively.</p></span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\"><p>UV &#2324;&#2352; SW &#2319;&#2325; &#8710;STU &#2325;&#2368; &#2342;&#2379; &#2350;&#2366;&#2343;&#2381;&#2351;&#2367;&#2325;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;&#2306;, &#2332;&#2379; &#2319;&#2325; &#2342;&#2370;&#2360;&#2352;&#2375; &#2325;&#2379; &#2360;&#2350;&#2325;&#2379;&#2339; &#2346;&#2352; &#2348;&#2367;&#2306;&#2342;&#2369; C &#2346;&#2352; &#2346;&#2381;&#2352;&#2340;&#2367;&#2330;&#2381;&#2331;&#2375;&#2342;&#2367;&#2340; &#2325;&#2352;&#2340;&#2368; &#2361;&#2376;&#2306;&#2404; &#2351;&#2342;&#2367; UV &#2324;&#2352; SW &#2325;&#2368; &#2354;&#2306;&#2348;&#2366;&#2312; &#2325;&#2381;&#2352;&#2350;&#2358;&#2307; 72 cm &#2324;&#2352; 42 cm &#2361;&#2376;, &#2340;&#2379; UW &#2325;&#2368; &#2354;&#2350;&#2381;&#2348;&#2366;&#2312; &#2332;&#2381;&#2334;&#2366;&#2340; &#2325;&#2368;&#2332;&#2367;&#2319;&#2404;</p></span>","options":["<span class=\"eqt\">45 cm</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">45 cm</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">40 cm</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">40 cm</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">50 cm</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">50 cm</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">42 cm</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">42 cm</span>"],"correct_option_id":2,"solution":"<p><img src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/other/er2307050001.jpg\"></p><p>C is the centroid which divides the median in 2: 1.</p><p>So, SW = 42 cm thus, SC = 28 cm and CW = 14 cm</p><p>And UV = 72 cm thus, UC = 48 cm and CV = 24 cm</p><p>Since &#8710;UCW is right angled triangle.</p><p>UW<sup>2</sup> = CW<sup>2</sup> + UC<sup>2</sup></p><p>=&gt; UW<sup>2</sup> = 14<sup>2</sup> + 48<sup>2</sup></p><p>=&gt; UW<sup>2</sup> = 2500</p><p>=&gt; UW<sup>2</sup> = 50<sup>2</sup></p><p>=&gt; UW = 50 cm</p>","marks":2,"section":null},{"question":"<span class=\"eqt\"><p>E is the centroid of the &#9651;ABC, where AB, BC and CA are 8 cm, 15 cm and 17 cm respectively. Find the value of BE.</p></span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\"><p>&#2348;&#2367;&#2306;&#2342;&#2369; E, &#9651;ABC &#2325;&#2366; &#2325;&#2375;&#2344;&#2381;&#2342;&#2381;&#2352;&#2325; &#2361;&#2376;, &#2332;&#2361;&#2366;&#2305; AB, BC &#2324;&#2352; CA &#2325;&#2381;&#2352;&#2350;&#2358;&#2307; 8 cm, 15 cm &#2324;&#2352; 17 cm &#2361;&#2376;&#2404; BE &#2325;&#2366; &#2350;&#2366;&#2344; &#2332;&#2381;&#2334;&#2366;&#2340; &#2325;&#2368;&#2332;&#2367;&#2319;&#2404;</p></span>","options":["<span class=\"eqt\">17/3 cm</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">17/3 cm</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">25/6 cm</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">25/6 cm</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">34/3 cm</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">34/3 cm</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">43/6 cm</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">43/6 cm</span>"],"correct_option_id":0,"solution":"<p><img width=114 height=108 id=\"Picture 13\" src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p19481/image013.jpg\"></p><p>AC = 17 cm</p><p>17<sup>2</sup> = 8<sup>2</sup> + 15<sup>2</sup></p><p>Now we can say &#9651;ABC is a right angle triangle where &#8736;B = 90&deg;.</p><p>Point E is on BD.</p><p>As we know, BD is circum-radius.</p><p>Circum-radius of &#9651;ABC = (Hypotenuse)/2 = 17/2 cm</p><p>BD = BE + ED & BE:ED = 2:1</p><p>BE = (17/2) x (2/3)</p><p>=&gt; BE = 17/3 cm</p>","marks":2,"section":null},{"question":"<span class=\"eqt\"><p>The area of &#9651; ABC is 44 cm</span><span><sup>2</sup>. If D is the midpoint of BC and E is the midpoint of AB, then the area (in cm</span><span><sup>2</sup></span><span>) of &#9651; BDE is:</span></p></span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\"><p>&#9651; ABC &#2325;&#2366; &#2325;&#2381;&#2359;&#2375;&#2340;&#2381;&#2352;&#2347;&#2354; 44 cm<sup>2 </sup>&#2361;&#2376;&#2404; &#2351;&#2342;&#2367; D, BC &#2325;&#2366; &#2350;&#2343;&#2381;&#2351;&#2348;&#2367;&#2306;&#2342;&#2369; &#2361;&#2376; &#2324;&#2352; E, AB &#2325;&#2366; &#2350;&#2343;&#2381;&#2351;&#2348;&#2367;&#2306;&#2342;&#2369; &#2361;&#2376;, &#2340;&#2379; &#9651; BDE &#2325;&#2366; &#2325;&#2381;&#2359;&#2375;&#2340;&#2381;&#2352;&#2347;&#2354; (cm<sup>2 </sup>&#2350;&#2375;&#2306;) &#2361;&#2376;:</p></span>","options":["<span class=\"eqt\">11</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">11</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">44</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">44</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">22</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">22</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">5.5</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">5.5</span>"],"correct_option_id":0,"solution":"\"<p><span><img src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/stubeimg/5b2fbf426218f9944dc45753e718034d.png\" />&nbsp;&nbsp;</span></p><p><span>\r<img src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/stubeimg/SSCT-MML-000382.png\"/>\r&nbsp;&nbsp;</span></p><p><span>\r<img src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/stubeimg/SSCT-MML-002052.png\"/>\r&nbsp;&nbsp;</span></p><p><span>\r<img src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/stubeimg/SSCT-MML-005579.png\"/>\r&nbsp;&nbsp;</span></p>\"","marks":2,"section":null},{"question":"<span class=\"eqt\"><p>&#916;PQR is an equilateral triangle and X and Y are mid-points of sides PQ and PR as per given in the following diagram. If area of the triangle PQR is 9&radic;3 cm<sup>2</sup>, then what is the length of the line segment XY?</p><p><img width=200 height=189 id=\"Picture 7\" src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p3002/image007.png\" ></p></span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\"><p>&#916;PQR &#2319;&#2325; &#2360;&#2350;&#2348;&#2366;&#2361;&#2369; &#2340;&#2381;&#2352;&#2367;&#2349;&#2369;&#2332; &#2361;&#2376; &#2324;&#2352; X &#2324;&#2352; Y &#2344;&#2367;&#2350;&#2381;&#2344;&#2354;&#2367;&#2326;&#2367;&#2340; &#2330;&#2367;&#2340;&#2381;&#2352; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2342;&#2367;&#2319; &#2327;&#2319; &#2309;&#2344;&#2369;&#2360;&#2366;&#2352; &#2349;&#2369;&#2332;&#2366;&#2323;&#2306; PQ &#2324;&#2352; PR &#2325;&#2375; &#2350;&#2343;&#2381;&#2351;-&#2348;&#2367;&#2306;&#2342;&#2369; &#2361;&#2376;&#2306;&#2404; &#2351;&#2342;&#2367; &#2340;&#2381;&#2352;&#2367;&#2349;&#2369;&#2332; PQR &#2325;&#2366; &#2325;&#2381;&#2359;&#2375;&#2340;&#2381;&#2352;&#2347;&#2354; 9&radic;3 cm<sup>2</sup> &#2361;&#2376;, &#2340;&#2379; &#2352;&#2375;&#2326;&#2366;&#2326;&#2306;&#2337; XY &#2325;&#2368; &#2354;&#2306;&#2348;&#2366;&#2312; &#2325;&#2367;&#2340;&#2344;&#2368; &#2361;&#2376;?</p><p><img width=\"200\" height=\"189\" id=\"Picture 7\" src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p3002/image007.png\"></p></span>","options":["<span class=\"eqt\">5 cm</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">5 cm</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">6 cm</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">6 cm</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">4 cm</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">4 cm</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">3 cm</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">3 cm</span>"],"correct_option_id":3,"solution":"<p>A line segment joining mid-points of the any two sides of the triangle is parallel to the 3<sup>rd</sup> side and its length is half of the length of 3<sup>rd</sup> side.</p><p>&#916;PQR is an equilateral triangle and let its side be 'a'</p><p>Area = (&radic;3/4) x a<sup>2</sup></p><p>9&radic;3 = (&radic;3/4) x a<sup>2</sup></p><p>a = 6 cm</p><p>XY = (1/2) x 6 = 3 cm</p>","marks":2,"section":null},{"question":"<span class=\"eqt\"><p>In a triangle ABC, AB = 33 cm, AC = 56 cm, and BC = 65 cm. From vertex A, a median AD is drawn that meets BC at point D. If G is the point on AD that denotes centroid, then find the length of AG.</p></span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\"><p>&#2340;&#2381;&#2352;&#2367;&#2349;&#2369;&#2332; ABC &#2350;&#2375;&#2306;, AB = 33 cm, AC = 56 cm &#2324;&#2352; BC = 65 cm &#2361;&#2376;&#2404; &#2358;&#2368;&#2352;&#2381;&#2359; A &#2360;&#2375;, &#2319;&#2325; &#2350;&#2366;&#2343;&#2381;&#2351;&#2367;&#2325;&#2366; AD &#2326;&#2368;&#2306;&#2330;&#2368; &#2332;&#2366;&#2340;&#2368; &#2361;&#2376;, &#2332;&#2379; BC &#2360;&#2375; &#2348;&#2367;&#2306;&#2342;&#2369; D &#2346;&#2352; &#2350;&#2367;&#2354;&#2340;&#2368; &#2361;&#2376;&#2404; &#2351;&#2342;&#2367; AD &#2346;&#2352; &#2348;&#2367;&#2306;&#2342;&#2369; G &#2325;&#2375;&#2344;&#2381;&#2342;&#2381;&#2352;&#2325; &#2325;&#2379; &#2342;&#2352;&#2381;&#2358;&#2366;&#2340;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;, &#2340;&#2379; AG &#2325;&#2368; &#2354;&#2306;&#2348;&#2366;&#2312; &#2332;&#2381;&#2334;&#2366;&#2340; &#2325;&#2368;&#2332;&#2367;&#2351;&#2375;&#2404;</p></span>","options":["<span class=\"eqt\">21.66 cm</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">21.66 cm</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">23.33 cm</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">23.33 cm</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">19.22 cm</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">19.22 cm</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">24.11 cm</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">24.11 cm</span>"],"correct_option_id":0,"solution":"<p>Sides of the triangle are 33 cm, 56 cm, and 65 cm.</p><p>We know that (33, 56, 65) is a Pythagorean triplet.</p><p>Therefore, ABC is a right triangle.</p><p>Median (AD) = Hypotenuse/2 = 65/2 cm</p><p>We know that centroid divides the median in the ratio of 2: 1.</p><p>So, AG = AD * 2/3 = (65/2) * (2/3) = 21.66 cm</p>","marks":2,"section":null},{"question":"<span class=\"eqt\"><p>In the following figure, M and N are the midpoints. If QR  -  MN = 10 cm, then find the length of QR.</p><p><img width=189 height=205 id=\"Picture 1\" src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p22768/image036.png\"></p></span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\"><p>&#2344;&#2367;&#2350;&#2381;&#2344;&#2354;&#2367;&#2326;&#2367;&#2340; &#2310;&#2325;&#2371;&#2340;&#2367; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306;, M &#2324;&#2352; N &#2350;&#2343;&#2381;&#2351;&#2348;&#2367;&#2306;&#2342;&#2369; &#2361;&#2376;&#2306;&#2404; &#2351;&#2342;&#2367; QR - MN = 10 &#2360;&#2375;&#2350;&#2368; &#2361;&#2376;, &#2340;&#2379; QR &#2325;&#2368; &#2354;&#2306;&#2348;&#2366;&#2312; &#2332;&#2381;&#2334;&#2366;&#2340; &#2325;&#2368;&#2332;&#2367;&#2319;&#2404;</p><p><img width=\"189\" height=\"205\" id=\"Picture 1\" src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p22768/image036.png\"></p></span>","options":["<span class=\"eqt\">20 cm</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">20 &#2360;&#2375;&#2350;&#2368;</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">5 cm</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">5 &#2360;&#2375;&#2350;&#2368;</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">10 cm</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">10 &#2360;&#2375;&#2350;&#2368;</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">15 cm</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">15 &#2360;&#2375;&#2350;&#2368;</span>"],"correct_option_id":0,"solution":"<p>Given that M and N are the midpoint so, MN = QR/2</p><p>And</p><p>QR  -  MN = 10</p><p>QR  -  (QR/2) = 10</p><p>QR = 20 cm</p>","marks":2,"section":null},{"question":"<span class=\"eqt\"><p>Find the length of the inradius of a triangle having sides 11cm, 60cm, and 61cm.</p></span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\"><p>11 cm, 60 cm &#2324;&#2352; 61 cm &#2349;&#2369;&#2332;&#2366;&#2323;&#2306; &#2357;&#2366;&#2354;&#2375; &#2340;&#2381;&#2352;&#2367;&#2349;&#2369;&#2332; &#2325;&#2368; &#2309;&#2306;&#2340;&#2307;&#2357;&#2371;&#2340;&#2381;&#2340; &#2325;&#2368; &#2354;&#2306;&#2348;&#2366;&#2312; &#2332;&#2381;&#2334;&#2366;&#2340; &#2325;&#2368;&#2332;&#2367;&#2319;&#2404;</p></span>","options":["<span class=\"eqt\">10 cm</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">10 cm</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">8 cm</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">8 cm</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">4 cm</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">4 cm</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">5 cm</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">5 cm</span>"],"correct_option_id":3,"solution":"<p>Sides = 11 cm, 60 cm, and 61 cm</p><p>Given triangle is a right-angle triangle as the sides are Pythagorian triplets.</p><p>Inradius = (P + B - H)/2 = (60 + 11 - 61)/2 = 10/2 = 5 cm</p>","marks":2,"section":null},{"question":"<span class=\"eqt\"><p>In the figure given below, AD = AC = BC and &#8736;CAD = 82&#730;, then find the measure of &#8736;A.</p><p><img width=192 height=162 id=\"Picture 2\" src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p8274/image005.jpg\" ></p></span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\"><p>&#2344;&#2368;&#2330;&#2375; &#2342;&#2368; &#2327;&#2312; &#2310;&#2325;&#2371;&#2340;&#2367; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306;, AD = AC = BC &#2324;&#2352; &#8736;CAD = 82&#730; &#2361;&#2376;, &#2340;&#2379; &#8736;A &#2325;&#2366; &#2350;&#2366;&#2346; &#2332;&#2381;&#2334;&#2366;&#2340; &#2325;&#2352;&#2375;&#2306;&#2404;</p><p><img width=\"192\" height=\"162\" id=\"Picture 2\" src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p8274/image005.jpg\"></p></span>","options":["<span class=\"eqt\">112.5&#730;</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">112.5&#730;</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">106.5&#730;</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">106.5&#730;</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">103.5&#730;</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">103.5&#730;</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">24.5&#730;</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">24.5&#730;</span>"],"correct_option_id":1,"solution":"<p>According to the question:</p><p>&#8736;CAD = 82&#730;</p><p>AD = AC = BC</p><p>Then, &#8736;ACD = &#8736;ADC = (180  -  82)/2 = 49&#730;</p><p>And, &#8736;ABC = &#8736;CAB = (180  -  (180  -  49))/2 = 24.5&#730;</p><p>Therefore, &#8736;A = &#8736;CAB + &#8736;CAD = 24.5 + 82 = <b>106.5</b><b>&#730;</b></p>","marks":2,"section":null},{"question":"<span class=\"eqt\"><p>Find the area of the hexagon formed after cutting the corners of the sides of an equilateral triangle of side 9 cms</p></span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\"><p>9 cm &#2349;&#2369;&#2332;&#2366; &#2357;&#2366;&#2354;&#2375; &#2319;&#2325; &#2360;&#2350;&#2348;&#2366;&#2361;&#2369; &#2340;&#2381;&#2352;&#2367;&#2349;&#2369;&#2332; &#2325;&#2368; &#2349;&#2369;&#2332;&#2366;&#2323;&#2306; &#2325;&#2375; &#2325;&#2379;&#2344;&#2379;&#2306; &#2325;&#2379; &#2325;&#2366;&#2335;&#2344;&#2375; &#2325;&#2375; &#2348;&#2366;&#2342; &#2348;&#2344;&#2375; &#2359;&#2335;&#2381;&#2349;&#2369;&#2332; &#2325;&#2366; &#2325;&#2381;&#2359;&#2375;&#2340;&#2381;&#2352;&#2347;&#2354; &#2332;&#2381;&#2334;&#2366;&#2340; &#2325;&#2368;&#2332;&#2367;&#2319;-</p></span>","options":["<span class=\"eqt\">2&radic;3/2</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">2&radic;3/2</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">29&radic;3/2</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">29&radic;3/2</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">27&radic;3/2</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">27&radic;3/2</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">20&radic;3/2</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">20&radic;3/2</span>"],"correct_option_id":2,"solution":"<p><img width=143 height=133 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p1084/image001.jpg\"></p><p>The diagram will be as shown in the figure.</p><p>Side of hexagon = 1/3 of side of &#916;</p><p>side of hexagon = 1*9/3 = 3cm</p><p>Area of hexagon = 6*&radic;3*a<sup>2</sup>/4</p><p>a= 3</p><p>Area = 6*&radic;3*3*3/4 = 27&radic;3/2</p>","marks":2,"section":null},{"question":"<span class=\"eqt\"><p>In an isosceles triangle JKL, JK = JL = X cm, and KL = 8 cm. From J, a median is drawn to KL that meets KL at M. If JM = 6 cm, then find the value of X.</p></span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\"><p>&#2319;&#2325; &#2360;&#2350;&#2342;&#2381;&#2357;&#2367;&#2348;&#2366;&#2361;&#2369; &#2340;&#2381;&#2352;&#2367;&#2349;&#2369;&#2332; JKL &#2350;&#2375;&#2306;, JK = JL = X cm &#2324;&#2352; KL = 8 cm &#2361;&#2376;&#2404; J &#2360;&#2375;, KL &#2325;&#2368; &#2323;&#2352; &#2319;&#2325; &#2350;&#2366;&#2343;&#2381;&#2351;&#2367;&#2325;&#2366; &#2326;&#2368;&#2306;&#2330;&#2368; &#2332;&#2366;&#2340;&#2368; &#2361;&#2376; &#2332;&#2379; KL &#2360;&#2375; M &#2346;&#2352; &#2350;&#2367;&#2354;&#2340;&#2368; &#2361;&#2376;&#2404; &#2351;&#2342;&#2367; JM = 6 cm &#2361;&#2376;, &#2340;&#2379; X &#2325;&#2366; &#2350;&#2366;&#2344; &#2332;&#2381;&#2334;&#2366;&#2340; &#2325;&#2368;&#2332;&#2367;&#2319;&#2404;</p></span>","options":["<span class=\"eqt\">2&radic;5 cm</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">2&radic;5 cm</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">&radic;13 cm</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">&radic;13 cm</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">5&radic;2 cm</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">5&radic;2 cm</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">2&radic;13 cm</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">2&radic;13 cm</span>"],"correct_option_id":3,"solution":"<p><img width=223 height=191 id=\"Picture 1\" src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p23087/image037.png\"></p><p>We know that the median drawn to the base is perpendicular to the base.</p><p>And KM = KL/2 = 8/2 = 4 cm</p><p>In &#916; JKM,</p><p><img width=112 height=20 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p23087/image038.png\"></p><p><img width=87 height=20 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p23087/image039.png\"></p><p><img width=60 height=21 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p23087/image040.png\"></p><p><img width=85 height=21 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p23087/image041.png\"></p>","marks":2,"section":null},{"question":"<span class=\"eqt\"><p>In &#916;WXY, Z is a point on XY such that &#8736;XWZ = &#8736;YWZ. If WX = 9 cm, WY = 14 cm, and XY = 20 cm, then the length of XZ is: (Up to two correct decimals)</p></span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\"><p>&#916; WXY &#2350;&#2375;&#2306;, &#2348;&#2367;&#2306;&#2342;&#2369; Z, XY &#2346;&#2352; &#2311;&#2360; &#2346;&#2381;&#2352;&#2325;&#2366;&#2352; &#2361;&#2376; &#2325;&#2367; &#8736;XWZ = &#8736;YWZ &#2361;&#2376;&#2404; &#2351;&#2342;&#2367; WX = 9 cm, WY = 14 cm, &#2324;&#2352; XY = 20 cm &#2361;&#2376;, &#2340;&#2379; XZ &#2325;&#2368; &#2354;&#2306;&#2348;&#2366;&#2312; &#2361;&#2376;: (&#2342;&#2379; &#2342;&#2358;&#2350;&#2354;&#2357; &#2340;&#2325; &#2360;&#2361;&#2368;)</p></span>","options":["<span class=\"eqt\">7.83 cm</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">7.83 cm</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">9.13 cm</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">9.13 cm</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">8.12 cm</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">8.12 cm</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">6.98 cm</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">6.98 cm</span>"],"correct_option_id":0,"solution":"<p><img width=262 height=200 id=\"Picture 5\" src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p18728/image004.jpg\"></p><p>Let, XZ = A cm</p><p>YZ = (20  -  A) cm</p><p>Given, &#8736;XWZ = &#8736;YWZ</p><p>So, WZ must be the bisector of &#8736;XWY.</p><p>By angle bisector theorem,</p><p>WX/XZ = WY/YZ</p><p>9/A = 14/ (20  -  A)</p><p>180  -  9A = 14A</p><p>23A = 180</p><p>A = 180/23</p><p>A = 7.826 = 7.83</p>","marks":2,"section":null},{"question":"<span class=\"eqt\"><p>&#916; WYX is a right-angled triangle, right angle at Y. YZ is perpendicular to XW such that XZ = 2.4 cm, and ZW = 6.5 cm. The length (in cm) of XY lies between:</p></span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\"><p>&#916; WYX &#2319;&#2325; &#2360;&#2350;&#2325;&#2379;&#2339; &#2340;&#2381;&#2352;&#2367;&#2349;&#2369;&#2332; &#2361;&#2376; &#2324;&#2352; &#2351;&#2361; Y &#2346;&#2352; &#2360;&#2350;&#2325;&#2379;&#2339; &#2361;&#2376;&#2404; YZ, XW &#2346;&#2352; &#2311;&#2360; &#2346;&#2381;&#2352;&#2325;&#2366;&#2352; &#2354;&#2306;&#2348;&#2357;&#2340; &#2361;&#2376; &#2325;&#2367; XZ = 2.4 cm &#2324;&#2352; ZW = 6.5 cm &#2361;&#2376;&#2404; XY &#2325;&#2368; &#2354;&#2306;&#2348;&#2366;&#2312; (cm &#2350;&#2375;&#2306;) ____ &#2325;&#2375; &#2348;&#2368;&#2330; &#2361;&#2376;&#2404;</p></span>","options":["<span class=\"eqt\">3 and 4</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">3 &#2324;&#2352; 4</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">6 and 8</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">6 &#2324;&#2352; 8</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">8 and 10</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">8 &#2324;&#2352; 10</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">4 and 6</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">4 &#2324;&#2352; 6</span>"],"correct_option_id":3,"solution":"<p><img width=279 height=229 id=\"Picture 1\" src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p23664/image002.png\"></p><p>Since YZ is perpendicular to WX.</p><p>So, YX<sup>2</sup> = XZ * XW</p><p>XY<sup>2</sup> = 2.4 * 8.9</p><p>XY = &radic;21.36</p><p>XY = 4.6 (approx.)</p><p>So, the value of XY lies between 4 and 6 cm.</p>","marks":2,"section":null},{"question":"<span class=\"eqt\"><p>Which option with given sides forms a triangle?</p></span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\"><p>&#2342;&#2368; &#2327;&#2312; &#2349;&#2369;&#2332;&#2366;&#2323;&#2306; &#2357;&#2366;&#2354;&#2366; &#2325;&#2380;&#2344;-&#2360;&#2366; &#2357;&#2367;&#2325;&#2354;&#2381;&#2346; &#2340;&#2381;&#2352;&#2367;&#2349;&#2369;&#2332; &#2325;&#2366; &#2344;&#2367;&#2352;&#2381;&#2350;&#2366;&#2339; &#2325;&#2352;&#2340;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;?</p></span>","options":["<span class=\"eqt\">100, 200, 300</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">100, 200, 300</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">8, 22, 9</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">8, 22, 9</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">4, 2, 6</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">4, 2, 6</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">18, 16, 19</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">18, 16, 19</span>"],"correct_option_id":3,"solution":"<p>We know that sum of any two sides of a triangle is always greater than the third side.</p><p>From option a, 100 + 200 = 300 (not satisfying condition)</p><p>From option b, 8 + 9 = 17 &lt; 22 (not satisfying condition)</p><p>From option c, 4 + 2 = 6 (not satisfying condition)</p><p>From option d, 18 + 16 = 34 &gt; 19</p><p>18 + 19 = 37 &gt; 16</p><p>16 + 19 = 35 &gt; 18</p><p>Satisfying the conditions.</p>","marks":2,"section":null},{"question":"<span class=\"eqt\"><p><div>&nbsp;If in &#916; DEF and &#916; PQR,&nbsp;<div style=\"display: inline-block;position: relative;vertical-align: middle;\"><span style=\"text-align:center;display: block; padding: 0;\">DE</span><span style=\"display: block; padding: 0;position: absolute; top: 0em; display: none;letter-spacing: -0.1em;\">_________</span><span style=\"display: block; padding: 0;border-top: thin solid black; text-align:center\">PQ</span></div>&nbsp;=&nbsp;<div style=\"display: inline-block;position: relative;vertical-align: middle;\"><span style=\"text-align:center;display: block; padding: 0;\">FE</span><span style=\"display: block; padding: 0;position: absolute; top: 0em; display: none;letter-spacing: -0.1em;\">_________</span><span style=\"display: block; padding: 0;border-top: thin solid black; text-align:center\">RQ</span></div>&nbsp;, then they will be similar when:&nbsp;</div></p><p></p></span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\"><p><div>&#2351;&#2342;&#2367; &#916; DEF &#2324;&#2352; &#916; PQR &#2350;&#2375;&#2306;,  <div style=\"display: inline-block;position: relative;vertical-align: middle;\"><span style=\"text-align:center;display: block; padding: 0;\">DE</span><span style=\"display: block; padding: 0;position: absolute; top: 0em; display: none;letter-spacing: -0.1em;\">_________</span><span style=\"display: block; padding: 0;border-top: thin solid black; text-align:center\">PQ</span></div>&nbsp;=&nbsp;<div style=\"display: inline-block;position: relative;vertical-align: middle;\"><span style=\"text-align:center;display: block; padding: 0;\">FE</span><span style=\"display: block; padding: 0;position: absolute; top: 0em; display: none;letter-spacing: -0.1em;\">_________</span><span style=\"display: block; padding: 0;border-top: thin solid black; text-align:center\">RQ</span></div>&#2361;&#2376;&#2306;, &#2340;&#2379; &#2357;&#2375; &#2360;&#2350;&#2352;&#2370;&#2346; &#2361;&#2379;&#2306;&#2327;&#2375;, &#2351;&#2342;&#2367; ______ &#2361;&#2379;&#2404;</div></p></span>","options":["<span class=\"eqt\">&#8736; D = &#8736; P</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">&#8736; D = &#8736; P</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">&#8736; D = &#8736; R</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">&#8736; D = &#8736; R</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">&#8736; E = &#8736; R</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">&#8736; E = &#8736; R</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">&#8736; E = &#8736; Q</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">&#8736; E = &#8736; Q</span>"],"correct_option_id":3,"solution":"<p>DE/PQ = FE/RQ</p><p>DE/EF = PQ/QR</p><p>So, &#916; DEF and &#916; PQR will be similar when &#8736; E = &#8736; Q</p>","marks":2,"section":null}]}